From 46900b1f0b5fa3884a9ff9895c9526dc6bc9286d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 11:26:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay: deterministic cross-architecture rooms, state
 instrumentation, AR-block logging, launcher fits small screens (v1.5.10)

A macOS ARM64 host and a Windows x64 guest desynced on v1.5.9. The host
sends its CPU core over NetPlay; a build that cannot construct that core
silently falls back to its own JIT (PowerPC.cpp), so the room ran two
different recompilers. Different cores split blocks differently, the
emulated tick only advances at block ends, and XD reads the time base:
its GBA link key (OSGetTick, 0x8002d430) differed by exactly the observed
48-cycle skew / 12, and its battle RNG seed is time-derived at boot.

- Clients send their CPU architecture at connect; a host whose room mixes
  x86_64 and arm64 puts every player on the Cached Interpreter (identical
  timing and arithmetic on all four builds) and says so in chat. Same-arch
  rooms are untouched. NETPLAY_FORCE_COMMON_CORE_ON_MIXED_ARCH opts out.
- Guest-side loud fallback when a received core is unavailable.
- accurate_fmadds was never serialized (always false on guests): forced
  on and put on the wire. MAIN_ACCURATE_CPU_CACHE, MAIN_GBA_PRACTICE_DUMMY
  (local GBA input injection) and MAIN_GPU_DETERMINISM_MODE pinned in the
  netplay layer. -ffp-contract=off for the interpreter cores.
- Interpreter cores on ARM64 hosts without FEAT_AFP flush denormal
  outputs in software instead of letting hardware FZ flush inputs too,
  matching x86-64 FTZ; FEAT_AFP now detected on macOS.
- gba_detect: 'cpu' boot line (effective core, arch, every determinism
  setting), 'xd' state lines (RNG seed, JoyBoot LCG, battle-state CRCs,
  keyed by WRITE ordinal), 'ar' lines (active codes on every machine,
  send/receive checksums).
- Launcher content in a scroll area, first-show height capped to the
  screen; Team Editor capped likewise.
